test.yaml:14:14: free text of an outsider from the variable BODY (github.event.comment.body) is expanded into the program of sed: a value with a slash ends the command and the rest is a program of its own. GNU sed runs commands with `e` (`a/g;1e id;#`) and writes files with `w`. keep the value out of the program text: read it from the environment in awk (ENVIRON["BODY"]) or perl ($ENV{BODY}), or cut it down to letters and digits first [argument-injection]
test.yaml:15:14: free text of an outsider from the variable TITLE (github.event.issue.title) is expanded into the program of sed: a value with a slash ends the command and the rest is a program of its own. GNU sed runs commands with `e` (`a/g;1e id;#`) and writes files with `w`. keep the value out of the program text: read it from the environment in awk (ENVIRON["BODY"]) or perl ($ENV{BODY}), or cut it down to letters and digits first [argument-injection]
test.yaml:16:14: free text of an outsider from the variable BODY (github.event.comment.body) is expanded into the program of awk, where it can close a string and call system(). pass the value with -v name="$VALUE" and read it in the program as name, or cut it down to letters and digits first [argument-injection]
test.yaml:17:14: free text of an outsider from the variable BODY (github.event.comment.body) is the command that find runs with -exec: an attacker who controls the value chooses what runs. use a fixed command [argument-injection]
test.yaml:18:14: free text of an outsider from the variable TITLE (github.event.issue.title) is expanded without quotes in find: the shell splits it into words, so it can add an option such as -exec. quote it, and give it as the argument of an option such as -name [argument-injection]
test.yaml:19:14: free text of an outsider from the variable TITLE (github.event.issue.title) is a word of find where a predicate can stand: a value that starts with a dash, such as -delete or -exec, is read as one. give the value as the operand of a predicate (-name "$VALUE") or put it before the paths [argument-injection]
test.yaml:20:14: free text of an outsider from the variable BODY (github.event.comment.body) starts a word of curl: a value that starts with a dash is an option, and options of this command can run code or write files (--output, -o, --upload-pack). put -- before the value, or give the value as the argument of an option [argument-injection]
test.yaml:21:14: free text of an outsider from the variable TITLE (github.event.issue.title) starts a word of git clone: a value that starts with a dash is an option, and options of this command can run code or write files (--output, -o, --upload-pack). put -- before the value, or give the value as the argument of an option [argument-injection]
